`Magma.revF31705aBad` holds the `24` clone members the subclones miss -- exactly the ones
that do generate `◇`. A target refuted by all of them is therefore not term-structural
from `1705`, over finite magmas and hence over all of them.

This file is generated by `revemit.py`.
